2991. Top Three Wineries
Table: Wines
Column Name	Type
winery	varchar
year	int
quantity	int

There is no primary key for this table.

Each row represents the quantity of wine produced by a winery in a specific year.

A winery can appear in multiple years.

Definition

For each year, a winery’s total production is the sum of quantities produced by that winery in that year.

Task

Write an SQL query to report the top three wineries for each year based on their total wine production.

If there are fewer than three wineries in a year, return all of them.

Return the result table ordered by:

year in ascending order

total_quantity in descending order

winery in ascending order

Output Format

Return a table with the following columns:

year	winery	total_quantity
Example
Input

Wines

winery	year	quantity
A	2020	100
A	2020	50
B	2020	120
C	2020	80
D	2020	60
A	2021	200
B	2021	180
C	2021	220
Output
year	winery	total_quantity
2020	B	120
2020	A	150
2020	C	80
2021	C	220
2021	A	200
2021	B	180

Solution 1
==========
WITH totals AS (
  SELECT
    year,
    winery,
    SUM(quantity) AS total_quantity
  FROM Wines
  GROUP BY year, winery
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT
    year,
    winery,
    total_quantity,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
      PARTITION BY year
      ORDER BY total_quantity DESC, winery ASC
    ) AS rn
  FROM totals
)
SELECT
  year,
  winery,
  total_quantity
FROM ranked
WHERE rn <= 3
ORDER BY year ASC, total_quantity DESC, winery ASC;

Solution 2
===========
SELECT
  t.year,
  t.winery,
  t.total_quantity
FROM (
  SELECT year, winery, SUM(quantity) AS total_quantity
  FROM Wines
  GROUP BY year, winery
) t
WHERE (
  SELECT COUNT(*)
  FROM (
    SELECT year, winery, SUM(quantity) AS total_quantity
    FROM Wines
    GROUP BY year, winery
  ) t2
  WHERE t2.year = t.year
    AND (
      t2.total_quantity > t.total_quantity
      OR (t2.total_quantity = t.total_quantity AND t2.winery < t.winery)
    )
) < 3
ORDER BY t.year ASC, t.total_quantity DESC, t.winery ASC;

Solution 3
==========
SELECT
  t.year,
  t.winery,
  t.total_quantity
FROM (
  SELECT year, winery, SUM(quantity) AS total_quantity
  FROM Wines
  GROUP BY year, winery
) t
LEFT JOIN (
  SELECT year, winery, SUM(quantity) AS total_quantity
  FROM Wines
  GROUP BY year, winery
) t2
  ON t2.year = t.year
 AND (
   t2.total_quantity > t.total_quantity
   OR (t2.total_quantity = t.total_quantity AND t2.winery < t.winery)
 )
GROUP BY t.year, t.winery, t.total_quantity
HAVING COUNT(t2.winery) < 3
ORDER BY t.year ASC, t.total_quantity DESC, t.winery ASC;
